Z||000000||bHooper||04-10-2000||11:22 AM||||does anyone know how much i should torque the bolts on the flywheel to?  also on the tranny when it is bolted to the engine?<P>is there a easy source for this kind of technical info?  the haynes/chiltons book is really lame when it comes to specifications.<P>thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||04-10-2000||02:05 PM||||84 fiero auto<BR>lower transaxle to engine bolts 55lb ft<BR>coverter to flywheel bolts 35 lb ft<BR>support bracket to transaxle 37lb ft<P>for stick same as above plus<BR>transaxle mounts to cradle nuts rear 18lb ft, front 36lb ft<P>bolt flywheel to crankshaft 44 lb ft||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||04-10-2000||04:24 PM||||thanks for the info!<P>does this mean that i have to torque the entire tranny to 55lbs, when attahing it to the engine?<P>there is a shield, behind the flywheel (to the lower half and right of the oil pump), what do i do to this?  also, mine has a minor crack, is that a problem?<P>thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||04-10-2000||09:57 PM||||Do you have the four cylinder or the v-6?  <BR>those are the specs for the four cylinder.<P>If its the four, i have a sheetmetal type shield on the flywheel, that you have to remove when taking the starter off, i dont think its important if its cracked, aslong as nothing can be thrown into the flywheel.<P>If anyone has pulled an engine, can you assist, i just got the specs from my service manual for the torque info, it doesn't state much in installing the stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||04-11-2000||06:57 AM||||fspeeder... i need the torque specs for a 6 cyl 5 speed.  <P>as for the shield, it is cracked on the upper half of the piece that surounds the oil pump.<P>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||04-11-2000||09:06 AM||||Flywheel to crankshaft is 50ft/lb<BR>Transaxle to engine is 55ft/lb<P>I got this info out of my Haynes manual. Just letting you know its in there.<P>That little sheet of black steel acting as a shield is a pain in the butt. Make sure it is aligned perfectly in place BEFORE torqing the tranny down snug. If it is not in its place, you will have to do what I had to do, and loosen the entire tranny and pull it outwards 1/2" from the engine to align the smashed plate.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||04-11-2000||09:22 AM||||Thanks, 56.<P>Will try so tonight.<P>hoop||||reg||1
